  "id": "bereavement-program",
  "term": "bereavement program",
  "definition": "A bereavement program is an organized set of supports for people after a death, especially families, to help with grief and maintain continuity of care. In the source, it includes measures such as staff training, guidance on end-of-life and bereavement communication, follow-up contact, condolence letters, support groups, and psychological follow-up when needed.",
